Test alias module for wrapped libraries:

  $ make_dune_project 3.5

  $ cat >dune <<EOF
  > (library
  >  (name foo))
  > EOF
  $ touch foo.ml bar.ml

  $ dune build foo__.ml-gen
  $ cat _build/default/foo__.ml-gen
  (* generated by dune *)
  
  (** @canonical Foo.Bar *)
  module Bar = Foo__Bar
  
  module Foo__ = struct end
  [@@deprecated "this module is shadowed"]
  $ dune build

The generated interface is also a direct target when there is no handwritten
library interface. Mixed-case library names retain their spelling.

  $ mkdir ordinary
  $ cat >ordinary/dune <<EOF
  > (library
  >  (name mixedCase))
  > EOF
  $ touch ordinary/bar.ml
  $ dune build ordinary/mixedCase.ml-gen
  $ touch ordinary/mixedCase.ml
  $ dune build ordinary/mixedCase__.ml-gen

Wrapped transitions retain the alias for a handwritten interface and produce
compatibility modules.

  $ mkdir transition
  $ cat >transition/dune <<EOF
  > (library
  >  (name transition)
  >  (wrapped (transition "Use Transition.Bar instead")))
  > EOF
  $ touch transition/transition.ml transition/bar.ml
  $ dune build transition/transition__.ml-gen
  $ dune build transition/.wrapped_compat/Bar.ml-gen

An explicit root module has its own filename, independent of the library name.

  $ mkdir rooted
  $ cat >rooted/dune <<EOF
  > (library
  >  (name rooted)
  >  (libraries foo)
  >  (root_module root))
  > EOF
  $ touch rooted/bar.ml
  $ dune build rooted/root.ml-gen
  $ cat _build/default/rooted/root.ml-gen
  module Foo = Foo

The root module is also available for an unwrapped library.

  $ mkdir unwrapped
  $ cat >unwrapped/dune <<EOF
  > (library
  >  (name unwrapped)
  >  (wrapped false)
  >  (libraries foo)
  >  (root_module root))
  > EOF
  $ touch unwrapped/bar.ml
  $ dune build unwrapped/root.ml-gen
  $ cat _build/default/unwrapped/root.ml-gen
  module Foo = Foo

A virtual implementation's alias uses the virtual library's prefix.

  $ mkdir vlib impl
  $ cat >vlib/dune <<EOF
  > (library
  >  (name vlib)
  >  (virtual_modules bar))
  > EOF
  $ touch vlib/bar.mli
  $ cat >impl/dune <<EOF
  > (library
  >  (name impl)
  >  (implements vlib))
  > EOF
  $ touch impl/bar.ml
  $ dune build impl/vlib__impl__.ml-gen
  $ dune build vlib/vlib.ml-gen
